jianji runs the following third-party software and models. It does not include, link or redistribute them; each
is installed or downloaded by you under its own license.

- FFmpeg (Homebrew's ffmpeg-full), GPL-3.0-or-later as built there. jianji calls the ffmpeg and ffprobe programs.
- Python dependencies installed by uv (mlx-whisper, whispermlx, silero-vad, mlx-vlm, numpy and their dependencies):
  MIT, BSD, Apache-2.0, PSF, ISC or MPL-2.0 licenses.
- Models downloaded on first use:
  - Whisper large-v3-turbo (OpenAI, MIT), via mlx-community;
  - Qwen3-VL-8B-Instruct (Alibaba Qwen, Apache-2.0), via mlx-community;
  - wav2vec2 base 960h (Meta, MIT), via torchaudio, for English word alignment;
  - jonatasgrosman/wav2vec2-large-xlsr-53-{spanish,french,german,italian} (Apache-2.0), for word alignment;
  - Silero VAD (MIT).
- Apple Vision, a macOS system framework.

Test fixtures (tests/fixtures):
- golden.mp4 and runon.mp4: speech synthesized with Piper TTS (run as a tool, not included) using the voices
  en_US-ljspeech-medium (LJ Speech dataset, public domain) and es_ES-davefx-medium (CC0), from rhasspy/piper-voices
  (MIT). Picture and room tone generated by FFmpeg.
- face.mp4: from "Official portrait of NASA astronaut Jack Hathaway" (NASA JSC, jsc2025e068207), a work of NASA in
  the public domain. No endorsement by NASA or the person shown is implied.
- phone_broll.mp4: generated by FFmpeg (a Mandelbrot zoom and brown noise).
